ic in ordinary conversation?", "options": ["A great deal", "Quite a bit", "Somewhat", "A little", "Not much"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_09", "type": "text", "label": "Describe a recent moment when this topic forced you to choose between two values you both care about. What did you pick, and what did it cost?"}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_10", "type": "text", "label": "What is one widely repeated opinion about this topic that you think is too simple? What nuance is usually missing?"}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_11", "type": "text", "label": "If someone you respect disagreed with you on this, what is the strongest version of their argument you could offer on their behalf?"}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_12", "type": "text", "label": "What would ‘good enough’ look like for you on this topic in the next year—not perfection, but meaningful progress?"}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_13", "type": "choice", "label": "You can improve one thing in this domain with serious effort, or help three people in a smaller way. Which pulls you?", "options": ["The deep single improvement", "The broader smaller help", "I’d try to combine", "Refuse the frame", "Depends on who is affected"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_14", "type": "choice", "label": "A policy change would help many strangers but slightly inconvenience you weekly. Support it?", "options": ["Yes, strongly", "Yes, cautiously", "Need more detail", "Probably not", "No"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_15", "type": "choice", "label": "You discover a habit of yours has unintended harm you didn’t see before. What’s your first instinct?", "options": ["Change quickly", "Research more", "Feel guilty", "Rationalize", "Talk to someone"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_16", "type": "choice", "label": "How much do you weigh future people (you’ll never meet) in decisions that affect this topic today?", "options": ["A lot", "Some", "Unsure how to", "Rarely", "Not consciously"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_17", "type": "choice", "label": "When brands or leaders speak on this topic, what erodes your trust fastest?", "options": ["Vague virtue signaling", "Data overreach", "Hypocrisy", "Fear messaging", "Overpromising"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_18", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could only protect one—honesty, kindness, or effectiveness—which do you lean on when they conflict here?", "options": ["Honesty", "Kindness", "Effectiveness", "Refuse to rank", "Situational blend"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_19", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you experience this topic more as a private inner struggle or a public political fight?", "options": ["Mostly private", "More private", "Both equally", "More public", "Mostly public"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_20", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you update your views based on new evidence vs. doubling down?", "options": ["Update often", "Sometimes update", "Slow to update", "Rarely update", "Depends on the source"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_21", "type": "choice", "label": "Which risk worries you more in this area: being exploited, or missing an opportunity to help?", "options": ["Being exploited", "Missing help", "Both equally", "Neither—different fears", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_22", "type": "choice", "label": "When you feel powerless here, what do you usually do with that feeling?", "options": ["Channel it into action", "Numb or distract", "Talk it through", "Blame systems", "Sit with it quietly"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_23", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather be remembered as principled or pragmatic on this topic?", "options": ["Principled", "Pragmatic", "Both—contextual", "Neither matters to me", "I don’t think in those terms"]}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_24", "type": "text", "label": "Name one assumption people make about ‘people like you’ in this topic that is often wrong or incomplete."}, {"id": "goldtechsupportaccessdig_