eselfexpress_17", "type": "choice", "label": "When brands or leaders speak on this topic, what erodes your trust fastest?", "options": ["Vague virtue signaling", "Data overreach", "Hypocrisy", "Fear messaging", "Overpromising"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_18", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could only protect one—honesty, kindness, or effectiveness—which do you lean on when they conflict here?", "options": ["Honesty", "Kindness", "Effectiveness", "Refuse to rank", "Situational blend"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_19", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you experience this topic more as a private inner struggle or a public political fight?", "options": ["Mostly private", "More private", "Both equally", "More public", "Mostly public"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_20", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you update your views based on new evidence vs. doubling down?", "options": ["Update often", "Sometimes update", "Slow to update", "Rarely update", "Depends on the source"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_21", "type": "choice", "label": "Which risk worries you more in this area: being exploited, or missing an opportunity to help?", "options": ["Being exploited", "Missing help", "Both equally", "Neither—different fears", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_22", "type": "choice", "label": "When you feel powerless here, what do you usually do with that feeling?", "options": ["Channel it into action", "Numb or distract", "Talk it through", "Blame systems", "Sit with it quietly"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_23", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather be remembered as principled or pragmatic on this topic?", "options": ["Principled", "Pragmatic", "Both—contextual", "Neither matters to me", "I don’t think in those terms"]}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_24", "type": "text", "label": "Name one assumption people make about ‘people like you’ in this topic that is often wrong or incomplete."}, {"id": "goldlifestyleselfexpress_