ic in ordinary conversation?", "options": ["A great deal", "Quite a bit", "Somewhat", "A little", "Not much"]}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_09", "type": "text", "label": "Describe a recent moment when this topic forced you to choose between two values you both care about. What did you pick, and what did it cost?"}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_10", "type": "text", "label": "What is one widely repeated opinion about this topic that you think is too simple? What nuance is usually missing?"}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_11", "type": "text", "label": "If someone you respect disagreed with you on this, what is the strongest version of their argument you could offer on their behalf?"}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_12", "type": "text", "label": "What would ‘good enough’ look like for you on this topic in the next year—not perfection, but meaningful progress?"}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_13", "type": "choice", "label": "You can improve one thing in this domain with serious effort, or help three people in a smaller way. Which pulls you?", "options": ["The deep single improvement", "The broader smaller help", "I’d try to combine", "Refuse the frame", "Depends on who is affected"]}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_14", "type": "choice", "label": "A policy change would help many strangers but slightly inconvenience you weekly. Support it?", "options": ["Yes, strongly", "Yes, cautiously", "Need more detail", "Probably not", "No"]}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_15", "type": "choice", "label": "You discover a habit of yours has unintended harm you didn’t see before. What’s your first instinct?", "options": ["Change quickly", "Research more", "Feel guilty", "Rationalize", "Talk to someone"]}, {"id": "goldtravelstaycationsloc_16", "type": "choice", "label": "How much do you weigh future people (you’ll never meet) in decisions that affect this topic today?", "options": ["A lot", "Some", "Unsure how to", "Rarely", "Not consciously"]}, {"id": "goldtravelst