ic in ordinary conversation?", "options": ["A great deal", "Quite a bit", "Somewhat", "A little", "Not much"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_09", "type": "text", "label": "Describe a recent moment when this topic forced you to choose between two values you both care about. What did you pick, and what did it cost?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_10", "type": "text", "label": "What is one widely repeated opinion about this topic that you think is too simple? What nuance is usually missing?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_11", "type": "text", "label": "If someone you respect disagreed with you on this, what is the strongest version of their argument you could offer on their behalf?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_12", "type": "text", "label": "What would ‘good enough’ look like for you on this topic in the next year—not perfection, but meaningful progress?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_13", "type": "choice", "label": "You can improve one thing in this domain with serious effort, or help three people in a smaller way. Which pulls you?", "options": ["The deep single improvement", "The broader smaller help", "I’d try to combine", "Refuse the frame", "Depends on who is affected"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_14", "type": "choice", "label": "A policy change would help many strangers but slightly inconvenience you weekly. Support it?", "options": ["Yes, strongly", "Yes, cautiously", "Need more detail", "Probably not", "No"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_15", "type": "choice", "label": "You discover a habit of yours has unintended harm you didn’t see before. What’s your first instinct?", "options": ["Change quickly", "Research more", "Feel guilty", "Rationalize", "Talk to someone"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_16", "type": "choice", "label": "How much do you weigh future people (you’ll never meet) in decisions that affect this topic today?", "options": ["A lot", "Some", "Unsure how to", "Rarely", "Not consciously"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_17", "type": "choice", "label": "When brands or leaders speak on this topic, what erodes your trust fastest?", "options": ["Vague virtue signaling", "Data overreach", "Hypocrisy", "Fear messaging", "Overpromising"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_18", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could only protect one—honesty, kindness, or effectiveness—which do you lean on when they conflict here?", "options": ["Honesty", "Kindness", "Effectiveness", "Refuse to rank", "Situational blend"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_19", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you experience this topic more as a private inner struggle or a public political fight?", "options": ["Mostly private", "More private", "Both equally", "More public", "Mostly public"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_20", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you update your views based on new evidence vs. doubling down?", "options": ["Update often", "Sometimes update", "Slow to update", "Rarely update", "Depends on the source"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_21", "type": "choice", "label": "Which risk worries you more in this area: being exploited, or missing an opportunity to help?", "options": ["Being exploited", "Missing help", "Both equally", "Neither—different fears", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_22", "type": "choice", "label": "When you feel powerless here, what do you usually do with that feeling?", "options": ["Channel it into action", "Numb or distract", "Talk it through", "Blame systems", "Sit with it quietly"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_23", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather be remembered as principled or pragmatic on this topic?", "options": ["Principled", "Pragmatic", "Both—contextual", "Neither matters to me", "I don’t think in those terms"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_24", "type": "text", "label": "Name one assumption people make about ‘people like you’ in this topic that is often wrong or incomplete."}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_25", "type": "text", "label": "What is a constructive disagreement you wish more people could have about this—without collapsing into teams?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_26", "type": "text", "label": "If you could ask one question to the most powerful decision-maker in this space, what would it be—and why?"}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_27", "type": "choice", "label": "After reflecting, how clear is your own position on this topic?", "options": ["Very clear", "Somewhat clear", "Mixed", "Uncertain", "Intentionally open"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_28", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you want a close friend to challenge you on this more often, less often, or about the same?", "options": ["More often", "About the same", "Less often", "Depends on how they do it", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_29", "type": "choice", "label": "How likely are you to seek new information on this in the next month?", "options": ["Very likely", "Likely", "Maybe", "Unlikely", "Very unlikely"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_30", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you feel more hopeful, more concerned, or about the same compared to a year ago?", "options": ["More hopeful", "About the same", "More concerned", "Both hopeful and concerned", "I avoid comparing"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_31", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could fund one type of project in this area, what would you pick?", "options": ["Education", "Infrastructure", "Research", "Direct aid", "Advocacy"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_32", "type": "choice", "label": "How much does community (online or offline) matter for how you think about this topic?", "options": ["Essential", "Important", "Moderate", "Minor", "I think alone"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_33", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather improve your own situation first, or work on collective change first?", "options": ["Own situation", "Collective change", "Both in parallel", "Refuse the split", "Context-dependent"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_34", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you translate reflection into concrete next steps?", "options": ["Often", "Sometimes", "Rarely", "I resist planning", "I over-plan"]}, {"id": "goldmediapodcastsdeepdiv_35", "type": "choice", "label": "Final calibration: how representative do you think your answers are of people in situations very different from yours?", "options": ["Very representative", "Somewhat", "Not very", "I doubt it", "I actively don’t know"]}]$json$::jsonb,
  true,
  'Media',
  pc.id
from public.payment_categories pc
where pc.slug = 'gold'
limit 1
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

